export anchor HtmlTag:
    description:
        Sets which HTML element each instance of the component becomes in the
        HTML output. Emul has no other way to give an element meaning, so
        this is how a component becomes a button, a link or an image.

    identifier: htmlTag

    cssProperty:
        None. It is an Emul property that sets the element's tag name in the
        HTML output.

    values:
        - `<tag-name>`, any lowercase HTML element name, such as `button`,
            `a`, `img`, `h1` or `section`

    initial: div

    appliesTo: All components.

    voidElements:
        Elements that can't have content in HTML, such as `img`, `input`,
        `br` and `hr`, are void elements. An instance whose component has a
        void htmlTag can't have text or children.

    notAllowed:
        The tags `html`, `head`, `body`, `script` and `style` are not
        accepted, because the HTML output uses them itself.

    otherOutputs:
        The SVG and PNG outputs ignore htmlTag, with one exception. An
        instance whose component has the htmlTag `img` is drawn as the image
        named by its `src` attribute, sized and placed by `objectFit` and
        `objectPosition`.

    styling:
        The element's own default browser styling is always removed, so
        htmlTag changes what an element means, never how it looks. A `button`
        looks exactly like a `div` with the same properties.

    example:
        ```emul
        \\\
        component Avatar:
            htmlTag: img
            width: 48px
            height: 48px
            borderRadius: 50%
            objectFit: cover
        \\\
        ```
